  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}). No pair verb.\n\nUSAGE:\nたじろぐ describes a momentary hesitation or wavering, often psychological rather than purely physical. It implies a temporary loss of confidence or resolve in the face of something daunting.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜にたじろぐ (to flinch at ~)\n- たじろぐことなく (without flinching)\n- たじろがない (doesn't flinch - shows resolve)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ひるむ - to cower/flinch (stronger fear, more about backing down)\n- {怯|ひる}む - same as above (kanji form)\n- ためらう - to hesitate (more about indecision)\n- おののく - to tremble (stronger fear response)",
